# v5.2.2 (audit A9): how to cite the simulation. The version field is set by dev/tools/set_version.py and checked by dev/tools/check_versions.js.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this simulation, please cite it as below, with the version you used. The math and code of this simulation were engineered by
  Claude, an AI model made by Anthropic, from the concepts in Duke Johnson's book Better To Best and his related vision for eradicating
  extreme poverty while enriching cultures and supporting human flourishing. The model has not yet been reviewed by an independent
  economist; the full code is open for anyone to check, and expert collaborators are welcome.
type: software
title: Compassionism Framework Simulation
abstract: >-
  An open, in-browser agent-based model of the Compassionism framework (Creative Currency Octaves, Public Trust Foundations, Public Trust
  Housing, Social Zone Harmonization and the Citizens Internet Portal): 500 simulated adults followed for 20 or 40 years, with the programme
  and with no programme, on the same random draws, in three environments, reporting poverty, work, cost and prices. Every published
  figure is an average over 500 paired runs; harness.js reproduces them in Node.
authors:
  - family-names: Johnson
    given-names: Duke
    affiliation: Better To Best Research Hub
    email: BetterToBestResearch@gmail.com
  - name: "Claude (Anthropic)"
version: 5.2.2
doi: 10.17605/OSF.IO/QWTE2
url: "https://bettertobest.github.io/compassionism-simulation/"
